# Orbit — title + thumbnail formula (locked 25 Aug 2026)

Canonical doc + evidence: `00_Brand/Channel-Setup/TITLE_THUMBNAIL_FORMULA.md`.
vidIQ remains the scoring gate; this formula generates the candidates.

## Shorts titles — use one of these structures

| # | Structure | Real winner |
|---|---|---|
| S1 | Strange image stated as plain fact | Most of the Universe Gives Off No Light (121) |
| S2 | We Found [impossible object] | We Found Planets Made of Diamond (63) |
| S3 | Why [named subject] [contradicts expectation] | Why JWST Pictures Don't Match the Textbook (83) |
| S4 | What You Would [see/feel] [extreme place] | What You Would See Falling Into a Black Hole (56) |
| S5 | What If [unsettling concrete idea] | What If They're Leaving Us Alone On Purpose (52) |
| S6 | Is [X] [wronger than we thought]? — only if the wrongness is inside the question | Is the Universe Older Than We Thought? (57) |

**Kill test (all must pass):** can you draw it · subject named (no orphan "this/it") ·
no hashtags in the title · no series suffix · states/contains the wrongness.
≤ ~50 chars, image words first. vidIQ `type=short` ≥90.

Proven failures — do not write: abstract questions ("How Did Black Holes Get So Big So
Fast?" 19), superlatives without a picture ("The Hottest Nights in the Universe" 16),
subjectless cleverness ("Falling In Wouldn't Feel Like Falling" 5, "Would You Look Back?" 3).

## Long titles

One promise, search-phrase-first, no series suffix. vidIQ `type=long` ≥90, prefer 95+.

## Thumbnails — scene-first (Ben lock 25 Aug 2026 · EARLY_POSITIVE_SIGNAL)

1. **No Orbit character by default** — the strange object is the thumbnail. Thumbs without
   Orbit are outperforming; keep testing, but scene-first is the new default.
2. Text ≤ 4 words, states the wrongness, readable at 168 px. One focal object.
3. Orbit allowed on **max one** ABC variant as a small corner accent (≤ ~12% width, never
   covering the subject); it must be A/B tested against no-Orbit variants.
4. ABC = A object hero · B emotion/scale · C question text — all scene-first.
5. Wonder brand: no fearbait comps. Re-evaluate the Orbit-on-thumb call once an A/B test
   resolves with a clear winner.

## Shorts covers — never grab a fixed-percentage frame

A blind frame at N% of duration is **not** scene-first. It lands on Orbit close-ups and on the
clip's own burned-in captions (25 Aug: ~half of 44 covers had to be rebuilt for exactly this).

Score every frame in the clip and pick the best: penalise Orbit-orange pixels (harder in the
centre), near-white pixels in the caption band, a busy top band under the punch text, and
near-black frames; reward detail. **Auto-fit** the punch text — 118 px Arial Black overflows
1080 px on strings like "NIGHTS HOTTER".

Builder: `00_Brand/Channel-Setup/tools/build_scene_first_short_covers.py`.

This supersedes older "3 Orbit-on-brand variants" thumb guidance in kickoff docs.
